  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any sales stop at the 5% failure rate (results above 5% trigger only review and a corrective-action plan), which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%, while per-model rates go confidentially to regulators and to that model's customers but not the public. S5 sets a mandatory recall above 8 per 100,000 per model after regulator validation, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9; the review step has no stated time limit, so the recall timing is open-ended. S3 gives installed units 72 months for retrofit, which favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which is within the acceptable range and is the main concession to Halcyon."
 },
